anseatic League and the Kingdom of Denmark, ending the war that the Danish king Valdemar IV had…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-furstenwalde"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Fürstenwalde</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 1373</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Fürstenwalde of 1373 transferred the Margraviate of Brandenburg from Otto V of the House of Wittelsbach to Emperor Charles IV of the House of Luxembourg.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-turin-1381"><span class="enc-name">Peace of Turin (1381)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1381</span><span class="enc-snip">The Peace of Turin was concluded in August 1381 through the mediation of Amadeus VI of Savoy and ended the War of Chioggia between Venice and Genoa and their allies.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/union-of-krewo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/union-of-krewo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Union of Krewo</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 1385</span><span class="enc-snip">The Union of Krewo was an agreement of 1385 under which Grand Duke Jogaila of Lithuania agreed to accept Catholic Christianity and marry Queen Jadwiga of Poland…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-windsor-1386"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-windsor-1386.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Windsor (1386)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 1386</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Windsor was signed on 9 May 1386 between Richard II of England and John I of Portugal, renewing the alliance of 1373 after English archers had fought for…</span></a></li></ul></section>
